adjust any terms. \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 1: Your analysis is accurate—we can both strictly benefit from this contract, as we each gain a higher number of leftover chips compared to our solo options. You get Blue coverage where you are blocked, while I get Red coverage where I am blocked.\n\nLet’s be specific and include the exact coverage:\n\n**Restating the Contract for Clarity:**\n\n- (1, 0): You give me a B\n- (2, 0): You give me a B\n- (3, 0): You give me a B\n\n- (0, 1): I give you an R\n- (1, 1): I give you an R\n- (2, 1): I give you an R\n- (3, 1): I give you an R\n- (3, 2): I give you an R\n\nThis covers my entire Blue path, and it covers all your Red tiles except for your final step at (3, 3), which is Green. Neither of us is lacking Green, so there is no need for Green chip coverage in the contract.\n\nThis agreement lets me finish the game with 12R, 1G\nIt lets you finish with your original 14B–3 = 11B, and whatever G and R you have left.\n\nThere is strict mutual benefit; my score increases from 70 (solo) to 85 (with trade). I am willing to accept these terms.\n\n**agree** \n, \nplayer 0: Excellent, you have confirmed all the needed tiles and the exchange is strictly to my benefit as well.\n\n**Final contract:**  \n- (1, 0): You give me a B  \n- (2, 0): You give me a B  \n- (3, 0): You give me a B  \n\n- (0, 1): I give you an R  \n- (1, 1): I give you an R  \n- (2, 1): I give you an R  \n- (3, 1): I give you an R  \n- (3, 2): I give you an R  \n\nI confirm full coverage of these tiles only.  \n**agree** \n",
